MVP Features (Phase 1)
1. User Authentication
	•	Mobile OTP sign-up (primary for Indian users)
	•	Google OAuth sign-in
	•	Guest mode for first-quiz try-before-sign-up flow
	•	Profile: avatar, username, grade/exam target selection
💡 Design Note: Minimise friction — new users should reach their first quiz in under 60 seconds from install.

2. Home Screen
Component
Description & Business Rationale
Daily Streak 🔥
Displays current streak count. Streak protection mechanic available for premium users. Primary retention driver — proven by Duolingo research to increase 7-day retention by 2.4x.
XP & Level Bar
Visual progress indicator. Fills with XP earned per quiz. Triggers level-up celebration animation — dopamine hit that encourages another quiz.
Daily Quiz Card
Pinned card with rotating daily challenge. Shared across all users — creates a common conversation topic and social virality.
Category Grid
Scrollable cards: GK, Science, Math, History, Current Affairs, Exam-Specific. Personalised order based on user history (Phase 2).
Live Leaderboard Strip
Shows user's rank vs. friends. Creates daily pull to open app and maintain rank.

3. Quiz Engine
	•	Multiple-choice questions (MCQ) — 4 options, 1 correct
	•	Timer per question (optional mode — toggled by user)
	•	Question shuffle and option shuffle to prevent memorisation
	•	Tap to answer → instant colour-coded feedback (green/red)
	•	AI Explanation card shown after each answer (correct or wrong)
	•	Difficulty levels: Easy / Medium / Hard per question, tagged at creation
	•	Session length: 5, 10, or 20 questions (user-selectable)
📐 Quiz Flow:  Start Screen → Q1 → [Answer] → Feedback + Explanation → Q2 → ... → Results Screen
⏱️ Target latency: question load < 400ms on 4G; explanation fetch < 800ms via AI API.

4. Results & Feedback Screen
	•	Score summary: correct / total, accuracy %, time taken, XP earned
	•	Mistake review: tap any wrong question to re-read explanation
	•	Share card: generate a branded result image for WhatsApp / Instagram Stories
	•	CTA: Play Again | Try Different Category | Challenge a Friend

5. Leaderboard
	•	Global all-time leaderboard (XP-based)
	•	Weekly leaderboard — resets Monday 00:00 IST
	•	Friends leaderboard (Phase 2 — after social graph is built)
	•	User's own rank always pinned at bottom of list

6. Core Gamification
Element
Mechanic
Motivation Psychology
XP Points
Earned per question answered, bonus for speed & accuracy
Variable reward — same mechanism as social media likes
Levels
XP thresholds unlock next level (1–100 scale)
Progress & mastery — sense of growth over time
Daily Streak
Consecutive days with ≥1 completed quiz
Loss aversion — fear of breaking streak drives return visits
Badges
Achievement badges (MVP Phase 2)
Status & identity — users display badges on profile

Phase 2 Features — AI & Social
AI Personalization Engine
	•	Difficulty Adjustment: after each quiz, the engine recalculates difficulty score per topic using a modified Item Response Theory (IRT) model.
	•	Weak Topic Detection: flags topics where accuracy < 50% over ≥5 attempts; surfaces on home screen as 'Practice Zone'.
	•	Quiz Recommendations: daily recommended quiz generated using collaborative filtering (what similar users found useful).
	•	AI Tutor Chat (Phase 3 preview): conversational follow-up — 'Why is this answer right?' resolved in a chat thread.



Analytics Dashboard (User-Facing)
	•	Topic-wise accuracy heatmap (7-day, 30-day, all-time)
	•	Speed trend: average time per question over time
	•	Strength & weakness radar chart across 6 subject categories
	•	Comparative benchmark: 'You scored better than X% of users in Science this week'

Phase 3 Features — Platform Expansion
	•	🎤 Voice-Based Quiz: answer questions verbally using device microphone; Whisper API for transcription.
	•	🤖 AI Tutor Mode: multi-turn conversational tutoring powered by Claude/GPT — explains concepts, generates practice questions on demand.
	•	📴 Offline Quizzes: cached question packs playable without internet; sync results on reconnect.
	•	📦 Exam-Specific Packs: UPSC, SSC CGL, JEE, NEET, CLAT — curated and expert-reviewed question banks sold as add-ons.
	•	🏫 School Partnerships: white-labelled portal for schools to assign quizzes, track class-level performance, and export reports.

🧩  User Flows
How users move through the product

Flow 1: New User Onboarding
#
Screen / Step
Key Design Decisions
1
App Install → Splash Screen
Show value prop in 3-second animation — 'Learn. Practice. Win.' 
2
Sign-up (OTP / Google)
Google one-tap preferred; OTP as fallback. Skip option leads to guest mode.
3
Interest Selection
Pick 3 categories from a visual card grid. Pre-selects personalisation without feeling like a form.
4
Profile Setup
Optional: name, class/exam, avatar. Skip-able — don't block progress.
5
Onboarding Quiz (3 Qs)
A fun 3-question mini-quiz in chosen category. Shows the core loop immediately.
6
Results + XP Celebration
First XP earned! Streak started! Sets expectation for daily habit.
7
Home Screen
Home with personalised recommendation ready. Nudge: 'Come back tomorrow to keep your streak!'

Flow 2: Taking a Quiz
	•	Home Screen: user taps a category card or the Daily Quiz card
	•	Quiz Lobby: select length (5 / 10 / 20 Qs), difficulty, timer on/off
	•	Quiz Loop: Question displayed → user selects answer → instant feedback → AI explanation (auto-collapsed, expandable)
	•	Progress Bar: visual indicator of question N / total at top
	•	Results Screen: score, XP gained, share card, next-action CTA

Flow 3: Daily Engagement Loop
Touchpoint
How QuizNova Hooks the User
Push Notification
Sent at user's preferred time: '🔥 Day 4 streak at risk! Take today's quiz now.'
Home Screen Anchor
Daily Quiz card always at top — one-tap to play, zero friction.
Post-Quiz CTA
'Try Hard Mode' or 'Practice Weak Topics' — next action always presented.
Leaderboard Check
Users open leaderboard to see rank — passive engagement even without quizzing.
Weekly Email Digest
Summary of week: accuracy %, rank change, weak topics, progress badge earned.

🏗️  Technical Architecture
How QuizNova is built

Technology Stack
Layer
Technology
Rationale
Frontend
Flutter (Android-first)
Single codebase for Android + iOS; fast UI; strong in India market
Backend / BaaS
Firebase (Auth, Firestore, FCM)
Zero DevOps for MVP; generous free tier
AI Layer
OpenAI GPT-4o / Claude 3
Explanation generation, question creation, weak-topic coaching
Analytics
Firebase Analytics + Mixpanel
Event-level funnel analysis; cohort retention; A/B testing
CDN / Media
Cloudflare R2 + CDN
Low-cost object storage; fast delivery for question images
Search / NLP
Algolia (Phase 2)
Instant question search; semantic similarity for dedup

Data Model (Enhanced)
Collection
Key Fields
Notes
users
user_id, name, level, xp, streak, streak_shield_count, interests[], lang_pref, created_at
Lang pref enables Hindi/English toggle per user
questions
question_id, text_en, text_hi, options[], correct_idx, explanation_en, explanation_hi, category, difficulty_score, source, reviewed_by
Bilingual fields; difficulty_score is float updated by IRT model
quizzes
quiz_id, category, difficulty_label, question_ids[], created_at, is_daily, exam_pack_id
is_daily flag pins quiz to Daily Quiz card
attempts
attempt_id, user_id, quiz_id, answers[], score, accuracy, time_ms, xp_earned, created_at
answers[] stores per-question time for speed analytics

user_stats
user_id, topic_accuracy{}, avg_speed{}, weak_topics[], rank_global, rank_weekly
Materialised view updated async post-attempt

