🎨  UI / UX Guidelines
Design principles and key interface decisions

Design Principles
Principle
What It Means in Practice
Mobile-First
All layouts designed for 360–414px width first. No horizontal scrolling. Large touch targets (≥ 48×48dp).
Speed = Respect
Every screen loads < 300ms. Skeleton loaders instead of spinners. No blocking modals before core action.
Celebrate Progress
Every XP gain, level-up, and streak milestone triggers a micro-animation. Learning should feel rewarding.
Reduce Cognitive Load
One primary action per screen. Clear visual hierarchy. No dark patterns.
India-Aware Design
High contrast for bright sunlight readability. Works on older Android versions (API 21+). Offline-tolerant.

Visual Design Tokens
Token
Value
Usage
Primary
#4F46E5 (Indigo)
Buttons, active states, progress bars
Secondary
#7C3AED (Purple)
Badges, level indicators
Success
#10B981 (Green)
Correct answer feedback, streak indicator
Danger
#EF4444 (Red)
Wrong answer feedback, time-running-out warning
Warning
#F59E0B (Amber)
Streak-at-risk alerts, near-deadline nudges
Font
Noto Sans (en) / Noto Sans Devanagari (hi)
Excellent Unicode coverage; free; renders well at small sizes
Base size
16sp
All body text; scale up for headings

