🚀  Go-To-Market Strategy
How we acquire, activate, and retain users

Phase 1: Launch (Months 1–2)
Target: Students in UP, Bihar, Delhi via organic social
	•	Create Instagram Reels showing quiz challenges ('Kya tum ye solve kar sakoge? 🔥')
	•	YouTube Shorts: '5 GK questions every Class 10 student should know'
	•	WhatsApp seeding: seed in student groups via college influencers
	•	Google Play optimisation: keyword-rich listing, localized screenshots
	•	Target CAC: < ₹30 via organic
Phase 2: Growth (Months 3–5)
Target: Scale to 100K DAU; launch competitive exam category
	•	Paid UA: Meta ads targeting Class 10–12 students (₹5–15 CPM)
	•	Referral programme: invite a friend → both get 7-day streak shield
	•	UPSC/SSC influencer partnerships on YouTube (₹10K–50K/video)
	•	Press outreach: EdTech journalists, startup media (YourStory, Inc42)

Retention Mechanics (Post-Acquisition)
	•	Day 1: onboarding quiz immediately → XP earned → streak starts → push notification scheduled
	•	Day 3: 'You're on a 3-day streak! Don't stop now.' + personalised weak topic quiz
	•	Day 7: first weekly leaderboard result + badge for 'First Week Champion'
	•	Day 14: upgrade nudge — 'Unlock unlimited quizzes + exam packs for ₹99'
	•	Day 30: monthly report card + personalised improvement data

